# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The fastapi image's /app is always overlaid by a bind mount at runtime
# (.ddev/docker-compose.fastapi.yaml: "../:/app"), so nothing copied in by
# the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` is ever actually used by the running
# container - only requirements.txt/requirements-dev.txt (copied and
# installed *before* that COPY) matter for the built image itself.
# Excluding everything below only shrinks build-context transfer and
# image size; it does not change runtime behavior.

# Live SQLite data - multi-GB and changes on nearly every request, which
# busted the COPY layer's cache on almost every build.
data/

# Secrets - never bake these into an image layer (layers persist in image
# history even after a later step "deletes" the file).
.env
*.pem
*.key
kalshi_devkey_private.txt

.git/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
venv/
.venv/
.vscode/
